{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario","id":1507262,"title":"Have you ever had your \"villain\" win scenario?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-02T21:29:28-07:00","id":1507262,"title":"Have you ever had your \"villain\" win scenario?","content":"I'm asking honestly here, I know most people write that the PCs should always come on top, but when they do stupid things like handing crucial information/artifacts to the villain &quot;just for kicks&quot;, I think there should be consequences, and I'm trying to experience in a &quot;Villain win scenario, you helped him, now deal with it&quot;, but I wanted to know how many of you have actually the experience of this kind of situation. I know many storytellers are afraid of trying this (especially inexperienced ones) because it would likely make the players unhappy, but I'm of the opinion that consistency comes first, so if you helped the &quot;villain&quot; get what he wanted, now you have to deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> Please share your thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T21:54:53-07:00","id":1507265,"title":"","content":"You could try to pull the old &quot;xanatos gambit&quot; where every solution to a scenario helps the villian even if they seem to ruin his plan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T22:03:11-07:00","id":1507266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507265#post1507265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could try to pull the old &quot;xanatos gambit&quot; where every solution to a scenario helps the villian even if they seem to ruin his plan</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems very interesting, the hard part is perhaps making their inevitable defeat fun to them lol. They actually loved the antagonist I created, and I suspect that is the reason they helped him so many times, but then now they want to act as if it doesn't mean anything, that they can win even after handing ALL POSSIBLE ADVANTAGES to him, I'm brainstorming how could I make it fun for everyone, because I see no way they can get out of this situation without major &quot;ST saving fiat&quot;. I think your idea is very interesting because it could give them the impression that they're actually winning (at least for a time).<br /> <br /> Do you have any experience to share about this sort of scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T23:04:23-07:00","id":1507268,"title":"","content":"1- Vampire players ARE the villains. <br /> <br /> 2-It's not DnD. There's never any world ending outside of a gehenna scenario. How powerful can an artifact really be? Somehow, going really big doesn't really fit with vampire games in my opinion, so a vampire who really does win the launch codes or daiblerizes an ancient can still be taken down after the fact. Ancient evils are no match for modern solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T23:29:03-07:00","id":1507269,"title":"","content":"It's perfectly fine for the antagonist NPCs to &quot;win&quot; if the PCs screw up. In my experience, when the PCs know they screwed up, they are disappointed if there are not consequences. As long as the NPC winning is &quot;fair&quot;.<br /> <br /> The challenge for the ST is running with this and creating the next challenge that allows the PCs to respond in a way that could give them a win. That does not mean they reverse their defeat as if it did not happen. But that they have a chance to still challenge the NPC in a way that makes sense given the new status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T01:01:44-07:00","id":1507272,"title":"","content":"(I was going to make a crack about the fact that the pcs <i>are</i> villains (anti-villains, at their best) but I was beaten to it, twice.) <br /> But yes, I would do that. A flat out victory where the pcs don't get anything from their efforts hasn't occurred yet, but often at least one antagonist still gets what they want out of the ordeal simply because they're more experienced, powerful and better connected... and then the pcs either focus on revenge or simply sell out. Vampires: go figure. <br /> <br /> Even over in D&amp;D I've had the players lose when it was the outcome that made sense, especially when they decided to be idiots (strangely, the bbeg did not put his plans on hold to politely wait for you to finish fucking around. Weird!) I don't stop them having fun if they decide to be silly, and I don't make the natural consequences the punishment at the end of it all, I just make it a hook for a sequel for them to fix their fuck ups. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T04:29:12-07:00","id":1507277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507266#post1507266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any experience to share about this sort of scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they genuinely have a good relationship with the &quot;villain&quot; what's to stop them from continuing the relationship? Like vampire's the kind of game where a competent, powerful and charming psychopath who kicks puppies and abuses children in is free time is not only OK but a character worth befriending if you want to better your position. The Villain's betrayal should be for a good reason with a reasonable cost-benefit consideration. I don't know why I would turn against the three stooges that got me everything I wanted for what sounds like very little cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T05:45:42-07:00","id":1507282,"title":"","content":"The tricky part of wanting a villain to win is you have to be sure what exactly you want from the win.<br /> <br /> Do you want the Villain to challenge the PCs, do you want the Villain to punish the PCs, or do you want the villain to just be a banal evil that makes the PCs good by comparison?<br /> <br /> The BBEG can pull a xanatos gambit, but not everyone is up for playing against that sort of an opponent. A lot of people play games to decompress, rather than amp up the mental exertion required to play against a xanatos gambit, let alone construct their own. Alternatively, not everyone can wrap their mind around that kind of planning, so to them it just comes off as ST said the bad guy wins.<br /> <br /> A better way would be a hybrid story where the BBEG has bigger plans, but the Coterie only interacts with the street level plans. So from the PCs point of view they might get some blackmail material on one person, steal some stuff from an estate, and vandalize a local nature area. Each of these actions is a separate storyline, and they are always paid for their efforts, it is only later on that it is revealed that the nature area was a shifter holy site which held warding in place, the random estate items were valuable artifacts to be trade to the Tremere, and the black mail allowed the villain to manipulate some mortal elections which in turn game him unparralled political power in the city. This way the BBEG wins, the PCs just don't percieve him as the villian until the end, and even then they might want to continue working for them.<br /> <br /> As for what happened in one of my games when a PC group &quot;lost&quot;.... The coterie was supposed to track a hunter who was using a local gang to soften up cainite targets. They managed to get some intel about a warehouse the gang was using. When they showed up, no one was around. Just a couple dozen empty wooden crates. The only thing inside was packing material that reeked of cosmoline and gun oil. The Players theorized that since the crates had cyriilic markings on them the gang must be moving drugs from eastern Europe. So, they planned to go over to the gangs main hide out and rip off the drug shipment, thinking it would be easy since they would only have a few pistols and maybe a shotgun to fight with.<br /> <br /> Well, the entirely mortal gang decided that uninvited guests was the perfect opportunity to try out their military grade weapons shipment from the Soviet Union. Between the entire gang wielding AK-47s with tracer ammo and the fact the PC somehow missed all the hints and thought that knocking down the front door was the best way to go, all but two members of the coterie were in torpor or dead by the end of the encounter. The mangled pair who managed to escape crawled back to their communal haven and opened an ice chest which had been delivered to their door with markings from a local blood bank. The hunter had a phosphorus grenade under the blood packs, when they players lifted the blood pack up, the safety bar sprung off and it went off in their faces. Needless to say, the game was done at that point.<br /> <br /> The villain doesn't need to go full xanatos to be a force of vexation and suffering for the players. Sometimes the players are their own worst enemy, the NPCs just reap the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T08:06:53-07:00","id":1507291,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this qualifies, but there was one time my cortorie went into a Tremere lair and one of the PCs had the &quot;brilliant idea&quot; to get a wolf that was trapped in a cage, the problem is that this wolf was a werewolf and he was very angry and to make matters worse, this PC instead of running wanted to fight with the creature, the others, despite having to force the situation, tried to help, but in the end it didn't work and we had to run, one of the ours died and the adventure became more difficult because the Tremere was more alert now, so the difficulty of some tests increased. In the end we only gained XP in this adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T09:42:09-07:00","id":1507295,"title":"","content":"Not in this setting as we are playing monsters of varying degrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T12:50:41-07:00","id":1507308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my experience, when the PCs know they screwed up, they are disappointed if there are not consequences </div> </div> </div>Yes, my thoughts exactly. By the way this is a phrase I often tell my friends who are starting to ST and are often afraid of making their &quot;players suffer&quot;. There's definitely a good level of sadism required to be a good ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you have to be sure what exactly you want from the win </div> </div> </div>The thing the &quot;villain&quot; wants (I know antagonist would be a better word choice) is to take control of the Kingdom they live. So it really fits the &quot;bigger plans&quot; you mentioned. The fact is that they helped an ancient being and now realize the folly of their actions, but it's too late. The logical development of the situation is the antagonist take power in the region and there isn't really much the group can make to avoid it, besides a kind of &quot;guerrilla warfare&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for what happened in one of my games when a PC group &quot;lost&quot;.... The coterie was supposed to track a hunter who was using a local gang to soften up cainite targets. They managed to get some intel about a warehouse the gang was using. When they showed up, no one was around. Just a couple dozen empty wooden crates. The only thing inside was packing material that reeked of cosmoline and gun oil. The Players theorized that since the crates had cyriilic markings on them the gang must be moving drugs from eastern Europe. So, they planned to go over to the gangs main hide out and rip off the drug shipment, thinking it would be easy since they would only have a few pistols and maybe a shotgun to fight with.<br /> <br /> Well, the entirely mortal gang decided that uninvited guests was the perfect opportunity to try out their military grade weapons shipment from the Soviet Union. Between the entire gang wielding AK-47s with tracer ammo and the fact the PC somehow missed all the hints and thought that knocking down the front door was the best way to go, all but two members of the coterie were in torpor or dead by the end of the encounter. The mangled pair who managed to escape crawled back to their communal haven and opened an ice chest which had been delivered to their door with markings from a local blood bank. The hunter had a phosphorus grenade under the blood packs, when they players lifted the blood pack up, the safety bar sprung off and it went off in their faces. Needless to say, the game was done at that point.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Hahaha this was fun to read. I think I've never been that much of a sadistic, I mean not ON THIS LEVEL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ancient evils are no match for modern solutions. </div> </div> </div>Well, first and foremost my story is set in the 16th century and second, with all due respect, I've been storytelling WoD chronicles for more than 2 decades, I know quite well the differences between a D&amp;D story and a WoD one. By the way in WoD we have artifacts that can utterly change the flow of the game, like the Eye of Hazimel or the Sword of Nul and I'm only talking about vampire here, because Mage and Werewolf have an even stronger focus on such things. What I'm proposing here is a healthy discussion about a situation that doesn't happen that often in most tables and approaches about how to keep things interesting for everyone even in a scenario where the PCs can't really completely overcome their antagonist anymore, because of actions they have taken before, etc. It's a discussion about a topic I'm proposing here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what's to stop them from continuing the relationship? </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops them in fact, it's just that now that they realize they helped a powerful ancient vampire that they have no hope of stopping by their own hands, they want to stop him at all cost. So, it's a kind of situation of action and consequence. They made their choice fully aware of what they were doing, but now changed their mind, but it's unfortunately too late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if this qualifies, but there was one time my cortorie went into a Tremere lair and one of the PCs had the &quot;brilliant idea&quot; to get a wolf that was trapped in a cage, the problem is that this wolf was a werewolf and he was very angry and to make matters worse, this PC instead of running wanted to fight with the creature, the others, despite having to force the situation, tried to help, but in the end it didn't work and we had to run, one of the ours died and the adventure became more difficult because the Tremere was more alert now, so the difficulty of some tests increased. In the end we only gained XP in this adventure. </div> </div> </div>Well, certainly it does in a way. Even though it was not like a &quot;total loss&quot;, the coterie did lose something, but that often happens in games, it's not unusual at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T18:14:27-07:00","id":1507343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507295#post1507295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in this setting as we are playing monsters of varying degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess it's better to oversimplify something, just because we don't want to add anything to the discussion. In any case, thanks for the contribution to the discussion....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T18:18:49-07:00","id":1507344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507308#post1507308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahaha this was fun to read. I think I've never been that much of a sadistic, I mean not ON THIS LEVEL.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hard part was keeping a straight face when I realized just how badly the entire group was misreading the situation and how poorly this could possibly go.<br /> <br /> At this point though, I treat situations like this as less me be sadistic and more that I am stoically saluting the PCs as they enthusiastically run right off a cliff.<br /> <br /> And yes, one of them did turn to me and say &quot;how does the smell of gun oil tell us they had guns?&quot;. Needless to say I didn't know how to respond to that for a couple seconds. Being the only person in a group with IRL experience in certain subjects can make RPGs a bit problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T18:55:15-07:00","id":1507346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507344#post1507344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hard part was keeping a straight face when I realized just how badly the entire group was misreading the situation and how poorly this could possibly go.<br /> <br /> At this point though, I treat situations like this as less me be sadistic and more that I am stoically saluting the PCs as they enthusiastically run right off a cliff.<br /> <br /> And yes, one of them did turn to me and say &quot;how does the smell of gun oil tell us they had guns?&quot;. Needless to say I didn't know how to respond to that for a couple seconds. Being the only person in a group with IRL experience in certain subjects can make RPGs a bit problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, it's really hard to keep a straight face in this kind of situation, especially in person. When I storyteller online it's easier though lol<br /> <br /> But I understand that's less about being sadistic and more with actions and choices having consequences, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T05:09:24-07:00","id":1507395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507308#post1507308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first and foremost my story is set in the 16th century and second...</div> </div> </div> </div>16th century is modern enough.<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1184_1680608002082_131\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1184\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1184\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1184&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Mr-Two decades of WoD experience, you probably should phrase your quandaries a little differently if you aren't so new to the game. Moving past that:<br /> <br /> Can the villainous NPC make any attempt to reconcile with the players? Reward them generously for their contribution? Publicly commend their efforts in helping him and thus setting in stone their position in the eyes of other vampires? Or god-forbid, move them with reason?<br /> <br /> If not, maybe you should encourage them to cut their losses and run, perhaps come back decades later when they're ready.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you don't want Villain to just end your players should conflict be garanteed, there's a few things you can do<br /> -the villain swoops up the player's backgrounds and alliances\u200b in the hopes that they won't do anything stupid until they see the error of their ways. Low-key hostage taking is always fun. <br /> -Before the villain tries to kill them in one fell sweep all he makes an error in calculation or a third party interferes to create a level playing field or allowing them enough time to flee. <br /> -Non lethal punishment. Maybe the big bad has a soft spot and thinks the players will come round to his way of thinking... after a few rounds of torture. Hell the big bad could even play the roll of the saviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T00:22:29-07:00","id":1507457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Non lethal punishment. Maybe the big bad has a soft spot and thinks the players will come round to his way of thinking... after a few rounds of torture. Hell the big bad could even play the roll of the saviour. </div> </div> </div>This is more like him. The thing is the case of the antagonist in my game is very <i>sui generis</i> as my players quite like him in a way, also because he's not a &quot;black and white&quot; kind of &quot;bad guy&quot;, but more like someone who thinks the ends justify the means. He had more than once the chance to destroy the characters, but he &quot;acts in mysterious ways&quot; (his demeanour is &quot;enigma&quot;, btw).They don't quite grasp his real goal.<br /> <br /> So, all in all I'm more interested in hearing about other stories you people have to share about situations where &quot;everything went wrong&quot; for the group and how you manage to make it &quot;fun&quot; for everyone, even when the antagonist wins or gets the upper hand, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T04:46:22-07:00","id":1507472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario#post1507262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking honestly here, I know most people write that the PCs should always come on top, but when they do stupid things like handing crucial information/artifacts to the villain &quot;just for kicks&quot;, I think there should be consequences, and I'm trying to experience in a &quot;Villain win scenario, you helped him, now deal with it&quot;, but I wanted to know how many of you have actually the experience of this kind of situation. I know many storytellers are afraid of trying this (especially inexperienced ones) because it would likely make the players unhappy, but I'm of the opinion that consistency comes first, so if you helped the &quot;villain&quot; get what he wanted, now you have to deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> Please share your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man talk more about the game, plot and villain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T14:59:41-07:00","id":1507518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507472#post1507472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man talk more about the game, plot and villain</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to summarize (a lot), the group essentially helped a Methuselah find and perform the ritual of Apotheosis contained in the <i>Sargon Fragment</i>, but that made the creature even more powerful than he/it was (absurdly so). So, even though he claimed he wanted to stop Gehenna and had &quot;good intentions&quot;, etc and thus helped the future Sabbath in their revolt against the elders. The thing is, he's now &quot;too powerful&quot;, to put it lightly, and the group realized (in fact the players were fully aware of the consequences, that's why I said the case is &quot;very <i>sui generis</i>&quot;) he wants to completely reshape the balance of power in Central Europe, and they think he's just starting. So, after some of his actions that led to the deaths of many mortals, they want to somehow stop him, because they think he'll never be satisfied. The thing is, even though the story is basically an elder story at this point (the story started in the 1200s), they have no chance of besting him and a part of the group wants to assassinate him.<br /> <br /> So, I said, the situation is very specific, but as I said, I'm not &quot;asking for help&quot; to manage my story, but more like proposing a discussion about how an utter loss can be made fun to the group. As I said, I'm very curious about your stories as well, when things went terribly bad for the group of players, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T02:00:46-07:00","id":1507564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507265#post1507265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could try to pull the old &quot;xanatos gambit&quot; where every solution to a scenario helps the villian even if they seem to ruin his plan</div> </div> </div> </div>This &quot;Xanatos gambit&quot; or &quot;Xanatos roulette&quot; pattern, attitude, method, or tactic could also very well be described and defined as the villian or the antagonist ( or a team of them ) as winning and succeeding despite setbacks and failures - and also no matter the chances and circumstances - in practically every encounter, situation, and also in regard to almost each event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T02:53:44-07:00","id":1507566,"title":"","content":"I feel if you're really going to try Xanatos gambit, you aught to write down a flow chart of what could happen, just to keep you grounded and away from the unreasonable and you can actually take a step back when players do something your villain can't account for. (plus like you can use it to appease your players if they think you're BS'ing them too hard) <br /> <br /> ..but also I'm not really sure of the applicability of leaning in too hard on Xanatos. <i>Gargoyles</i> was primarily aimed at kids, Xanatos was a cheesy villain who'd explain his actions all the time and would rarely press his advantage hard. VTM is more adult, and most vampires will use the time they metaphorically caught you with your pants down to metaphorically cut your dick off. MacBeth was a better villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T14:02:06-07:00","id":1507602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This &quot;Xanatos gambit&quot; or &quot;Xanatos roulette&quot; pattern, attitude, method, or tactic could also very well be described and defined as the villian or the antagonist ( or a team of them ) as winning and succeeding despite setbacks and failures - and also no matter the chances and circumstances - in practically every encounter, situation, and also in regard to almost each event. </div> </div> </div>It's a good point. At the moment the group is in a situation (caused by their own actions and choices) that there's just isn't much they can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel if you're really going to try Xanatos gambit, you aught to write down a flow chart of what could happen, just to keep you grounded and away from the unreasonable and you can actually take a step back when players do something your villain can't account for. (plus like you can use it to appease your players if they think you're BS'ing them too hard) </div> </div> </div>You mentioned something that I always make. As an aspiring writer (I'm yet to publish a book), I like to write this kind of things, like what the NPCs in general know and what are they up to and how their plans could be foiled and sometimes even their actions &quot;behind the scenes&quot;, because I don't really like to take &quot;too arbitrary decisions&quot;, one of the things I find more fascinating about RPG is that the story has this many ramifications of possibilities, it's always open and I try to keep it this way. By the way this is one of the reasons I often post these kinds of situations in a forum, to hear other thoughts, to explore the many possible ramifications the story can take as another way to let the &quot;RNG&quot; factor influence my writing, the direction the story goes, etc. <br /> <br /> PS: I'm also a great fan of Shakespeare and I love MacBeth, but I think perhaps Hamlet is my favorite play. I think Hamlet is one of (if not the) the best characters ever made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T14:09:37-07:00","id":1507603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .but also I'm not really sure of the applicability of leaning in too hard on Xanatos. <i>Gargoyles</i> was primarily aimed at kids, Xanatos was a cheesy villain who'd explain his actions all the time and would rarely press his advantage hard.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Just as an addendum, I think the term &quot;Xanatos gambit&quot; nowadays refers more to a narrative situation than to the original story. Just like the term &quot;Mary Sue&quot;, I don't even know the original Mary Sue character, but I know what the term means in a story context (like Sypha in Netflix's Castlevania series hahaha, I really hated what they made there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T14:52:13-07:00","id":1507605,"title":"","content":"I heard that the term Mary Sue came from a Star Trek fanfic back in the day that had an officer named Mary Sue and was super skilled and liked by the crew. To be fair I never heard of the term until a few years ago when movies like Captain Marvel and others came out and had to look up the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-06-2023, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T15:22:43-07:00","id":1507612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507566#post1507566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel if you're really going to try Xanatos gambit, you aught to write down a flow chart of what could happen, just to keep you grounded and away from the unreasonable and you can actually take a step back when players do something your villain can't account for. (plus like you can use it to appease your players if they think you're BS'ing them too hard)<br /> <br /> ..but also I'm not really sure of the applicability of leaning in too hard on Xanatos. <i>Gargoyles</i> was primarily aimed at kids, Xanatos was a cheesy villain who'd explain his actions all the time and would rarely press his advantage hard. VTM is more adult, and most vampires will use the time they metaphorically caught you with your pants down to metaphorically cut your dick off. MacBeth was a better villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair Gargoyles like Batman The Animated Series or X-Men didn't come across as simply aimed at children and had some well thought story arcs that still hold up well nearly 30 years later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-12-2023, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:14:06-07:00","id":1507621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507605#post1507605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that the term Mary Sue came from a Star Trek fanfic back in the day that had an officer named Mary Sue and was super skilled and liked by the crew. To be fair I never heard of the term until a few years ago when movies like Captain Marvel and others came out and had to look up the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had absolutely no idea where the term came from, only the vague idea that there was once a Mary Sue who was super skilled, cool, young, intelligent and seemed to enjoy the story's writer protection (I almost described Sypha's role in Netflix's Castlevania series lol). Nowadays, we see a lot of these characters by the way, especially when the people developing shows &quot;want to make a point&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T22:32:41-07:00","id":1507658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507612#post1507612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair Gargoyles like Batman The Animated Series or X-Men didn't come across as simply aimed at children and had some well though story arcs that still hold up well nearly 30 years later.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>X-Men The Animated Series</i> was great, positive and interesting ; and there was also of course <i>Iron Man</i>.<br /> These animated series are a nice and good introduction in regard to the particular comic book characters, and also as well an invitation to looking through and reading comic books in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T23:24:33-07:00","id":1507661,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm not knocking Gargoyles, which I first watched when I was in my early 20s. There are a lot of good cartoons for all ages, but it must be said that though the writers did well in giving stories and dialogue and the buttery voice of Keith David very much enjoyable for adults, they ultimately couldn't use firearms and had to settle for energy weapons because it was a &quot;Kid's show&quot;. Actually, I watched a bunch of western cartoons that I missed out on as a kid when I was in my early 20s. X-Men was great, spiderman was great, Superman's fantastic, Avatar's a masterpiece... and now my daughter's 3 and some of the stuff she watches is excellently enjoyable to me as I approach 30. (some of it is absolutely mindless trash, but there is gold there both in old and new cartoons) Bugs Bunny is timeless, Old Tom and Jerry is hilarious, Pink panther cartoon's more modern episodes aren't as good as the old but aren't half bad, Pocoyo is great, Bluey and Peppa pig are far too relatable, Masha made me cry... These are all certainly kids shows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back on the main topic, OP, what clan is the Big Bad? Like how I'd sort everything out for a Ventrue would be very different from how I'd sort things out as a malkavian or toreador.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-07-2023, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T00:09:46-07:00","id":1507664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back on the main topic, OP, what clan is the Big Bad? Like how I'd sort everything out for a Ventrue would be very different from how I'd sort things out as a malkavian or toreador. </div> </div> </div>He was originally a mighty Koldun, but since he made the ritual of Apotheosis (of the Sargon Fragment, with the complete support from the players, I need to add) clan became less important as he now represents the same level of threat of Baba Yaga/Ur-Shulgi/Goratrix/Mithras, etc. So, it's not really through direct confrontation that the group is going to stop him, problem is, a part of the group wants just that, even knowing their chances are very slim (one of my players used to play werewolf and he kind of likes the idea of &quot;heroic confrontation even against all odds&quot;).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T00:25:53-07:00","id":1507666,"title":"","content":"Alright, just let them die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T00:38:02-07:00","id":1507667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507666#post1507666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, just let them die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, that was unexpected I might add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T00:52:38-07:00","id":1508006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507518#post1507518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, to summarize (a lot), the group essentially helped a Methuselah find and perform the ritual of Apotheosis contained in the <i>Sargon Fragment</i>, but that made the creature even more powerful than he/it was (absurdly so). So, even though he claimed he wanted to stop Gehenna and had &quot;good intentions&quot;, etc and thus helped the future Sabbath in their revolt against the elders. The thing is, he's now &quot;too powerful&quot;, to put it lightly, and the group realized (in fact the players were fully aware of the consequences, that's why I said the case is &quot;very <i>sui generis</i>&quot;) he wants to completely reshape the balance of power in Central Europe, and they think he's just starting. So, after some of his actions that led to the deaths of many mortals, they want to somehow stop him, because they think he'll never be satisfied. The thing is, even though the story is basically an elder story at this point (the story started in the 1200s), they have no chance of besting him and a part of the group wants to assassinate him.<br /> <br /> So, I said, the situation is very specific, but as I said, I'm not &quot;asking for help&quot; to manage my story, but more like proposing a discussion about how an utter loss can be made fun to the group. As I said, I'm very curious about your stories as well, when things went terribly bad for the group of players, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you want a good idea of how a party can cope with an overpowered villain I have one word for you: Drachenfels<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:24:00-07:00","id":1508068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508006#post1508006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you want a good idea of how a party can cope with an overpowered villain I have one word for you: Drachenfels<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You made me curious, where can I find more information about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:09:43-07:00","id":1508236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want a good idea of how a party can cope with an overpowered villain I have one word for you: Drachenfels </div> </div> </div>I'm really not sure if this was meant with irony in mind, but to be fair, as one friend of mine who loves <i>D&amp;D </i>a lot, in the WoD it's much more common to have possible antagonists that you definitely can't defeat than in other games. I'm saying that, because it sounded like perhaps you meant that ironically, in the sense that I should look more at other games (isn't Drachenfels from <i>Warhammer</i>?(besides being a famous hill in Germany lol)).<br /> <br /> In the WoD, most of the time players aren't expected to really defeat the &quot;big baddies&quot; like Mithras, Baba Yaga, Goratrix, Ur-Shulgi, etc. Some books even mention that explicitly, like <i>Rage Across Russia</i>, that mention that the werewolves from the PCs aren't expected to really deal with Baba Yaga and her Zmeis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T23:35:36-07:00","id":1508250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508236#post1508236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD, most of the time players aren't expected to really defeat the &quot;big baddies&quot; like Mithras, Baba Yaga, Goratrix, Ur-Shulgi, etc. Some books even mention that explicitly, like <i>Rage Across Russia</i>, that mention that the werewolves from the PCs aren't expected to really deal with Baba Yaga and her Zmeis.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand in World of Darkness there is often distinctly the possibility of achieving a success on the social arena and also in regard to information gathering and knowledge seeking.<br /> Such victories and positive outcomes can definitely happen regardless of differences in power level and disruptive circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T00:28:57-07:00","id":1508252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508250#post1508250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand in World of Darkness there is often distinctly the possibility of achieving a success on the social arena and also in regard to information gathering and knowledge seeking.<br /> Such victories and positive outcomes can definitely happen regardless of differences in power level and disruptive circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I completely agree with that statement, in every way. In the WoD there's a great emphasis in politics, so to speak (not so much in Werewolf, but you get what I mean). You definitely can learn to use your enemy's enemies as a way to deal with your enemy or, as is more common, to learn to come to an agreement with your enemies, etc.<br /> <br /> One of the &quot;problems&quot; I mentioned is that a part of the group still want to go &quot;all out&quot; against an enemy that is completely out of their league. It's as if you're storytelling a game set in the British Isles and the group decided to take Mithras away from &quot;the throne&quot; or a werewolf group decided that they are going to fight Baba Yaga, even when everyone and the books themselves state they wouldn't stand a chance.As I said, it's a matter of choices and consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-13-2023, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T01:52:54-07:00","id":1508259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508068#post1508068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You made me curious, where can I find more information about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't realise that s simple search wouldn't turn up the relevant point: <a href=\"https://johnnyalucard.com/fiction/by-jack-yeovil/drachenfels-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Drachenfels | The Kim Newman Web Site (johnnyalucard.com)</a><br /> <br /> Drachenfels is a book, set in the Warhammer Fantasy universe\u200b, where a group of adventurers head out to tackle the Dark Lord. I won't explain any further as that could introduce spoilers for a rather good book by a very good author. I will point out that the lead character is a vampire which is why it should be of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 04-13-2023, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T17:51:16-07:00","id":1508310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508259#post1508259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I didn't realise that s simple search wouldn't turn up the relevant point: <a href=\"https://johnnyalucard.com/fiction/by-jack-yeovil/drachenfels-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Drachenfels | The Kim Newman Web Site (johnnyalucard.com)</a><br /> <br /> Drachenfels is a book, set in the Warhammer Fantasy universe\u200b, where a group of adventurers head out to tackle the Dark Lord. I won't explain any further as that could introduce spoilers for a rather good book by a very good author. I will point out that the lead character is a vampire which is why it should be of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm gong to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:40:29-07:00","id":1508575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario#post1507262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking honestly here, I know most people write that the PCs should always come on top, but when they do stupid things like handing crucial information/artifacts to the villain &quot;just for kicks&quot;, I think there should be consequences, and I'm trying to experience in a &quot;Villain win scenario, you helped him, now deal with it&quot;, but I wanted to know how many of you have actually the experience of this kind of situation. I know many storytellers are afraid of trying this (especially inexperienced ones) because it would likely make the players unhappy, but I'm of the opinion that consistency comes first, so if you helped the &quot;villain&quot; get what he wanted, now you have to deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> Please share your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh all the time.<br /> <br /> After all, bad endings are to be expected in a game where the goal isn't to kill the Prince or the Elders but survive their machinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T16:56:39-07:00","id":1508583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508575#post1508575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh all the time.<br /> <br /> After all, bad endings are to be expected in a game where the goal isn't to kill the Prince or the Elders but survive their machinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my thought as well. Unfortunately we see many instances in books where the coterie is almost predetermined to &quot;win&quot;, Darkening Sky is a good example by the way.<br /> <br /> Would you care to share any of your experiences with this kind of scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T16:58:34-07:00","id":1508584,"title":"","content":"Well, once in a Hunter's Hunted game; the players were mortal teenagers with some numia; it played out like a scene from <i>Nightmare on Elm Street </i>and didn't go well for the players. <br /> <br /> <br /> And not for Masquerade, but for Cyberpunk 2020's Night's Edge; in a war between two covens, the players, um, became casualties. The game system is a lot more lethal. However, once of the players, that was trapped in burning-building, burned to death, but his ashes weren't disturbed, came back (Vampires can do that in that system). <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1507268#post1507268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Vampire players ARE the villains.<br /> <br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ain't that the truth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:16:11-07:00","id":1508587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508584#post1508584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, once in a Hunter's Hunted game; the players were mortal teenagers with some numia; it played out like a scene from <i>Nightmare on Elm Street </i>and didn't go well for the players.<br /> <br /> <br /> And not for Masquerade, but for Cyberpunk 2020's Night's Edge; in a war between two covens, the players, um, became casualties. The game system is a lot more lethal. However, once of the players, that was trapped in burning-building, burned to death, but his ashes weren't disturbed, came back (Vampires can do that in that system).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ain't that the truth.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting story, but I have my doubts if there's a system &quot;more lethal&quot; than the Storyteller hahaha, I mean vampires, especially, are so easy to kill that it often makes me change some of the rules, Werewolves I'd argue are a bit tougher by default, but (beginning of the &quot;rant&quot;) I blame that almost entirely on power creep. Vampire suffered for being the first, then Werewolf and Mage seemed to want to show &quot;how incredible powerful/strong they were&quot; in order to boost their appeal. They tried to balance things a bit later, but then third edition basically fucked vampires with the bizarre rule of only using Fortitude to soak aggravated damage and vampires being destroyed even when there was still blood in their system, so vampires could be easily destroyed with a single claw attack or any decent magic attack from a mage, what in my honest opinion shouldn't be possible as vampires are normally known for being &quot;hard to kill&quot; in any legend and almost any RPG system (end of the &quot;rant&quot;)<br /> <br /> In Requiem, I think they made vampires a bit tougher to kill, but not by much and there was also a lot of power creep at play there. In any case, I'd love to read the stories you have to share.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ain't that the truth.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Not always...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T16:52:20-07:00","id":1508677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508587#post1508587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting story, but I have my doubts if there's a system &quot;more lethal&quot; than the Storyteller hahaha, I mean vampires, especially, are so easy to kill that it often makes me change some of the rules, Werewolves I'd argue are a bit tougher by default, but (beginning of the &quot;rant&quot;) I blame that almost entirely on power creep. Vampire suffered for being the first, then Werewolf and Mage seemed to want to show &quot;how incredible powerful/strong they were&quot; in order to boost their appeal. They tried to balance things a bit later, but then third edition basically fucked vampires with the bizarre rule of only using Fortitude to soak aggravated damage and vampires being destroyed even when there was still blood in their system, so vampires could be easily destroyed with a single claw attack or any decent magic attack from a mage, what in my honest opinion shouldn't be possible as vampires are normally known for being &quot;hard to kill&quot; in any legend and almost any RPG system (end of the &quot;rant&quot;)<br /> <br /> In Requiem, I think they made vampires a bit tougher to kill, but not by much and there was also a lot of power creep at play there. In any case, I'd love to read the stories you have to share.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not always...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to explain; but we found that Cyberpunk, 2020 vamps, died faster than Masquerade Vamps and but, Requiem vamps lasted longer than Masquerade vamps. It's like the Matrix; you have to experience it to understand; so CP:2020, roll 1D10 to determine hit-location. A, &quot;1&quot;, is a head-shot; if you do over eight-points of damage to a limb, it's useless and may be blown off. So, over eight-points of damage kills a PC or NPC. So, a 9mm pistol does 2D6+1 damage, so, there's over a 50% chance that one handgun round to the head will kill a PC or NPC. For vampires, that's not death, but they're immobilized and out of the game until they heal*; I hoped they aren't outside because dawn will happen. <br /> <br /> *Healing's tricky; a fledgling vampire will heal 4 points of damage a day (Mortals heal, like one point a day, maybe with a medical-roll) or they get 2 Bod-points of blood (humans have 1 to 10 Bod-points) that heals one point of damage. So even and ancilla or elder vampire, one round to the head and they're out. a 500 year old plus vampire, well, their skin has better stopping-power and you'd have to use a rifle.<br /> <br /> We did like WW:tA because of their Wipey-ness. They can wipe NPCs off the board. Since most of use were D&amp;D players, we understood Aggravated-damage as simply magical-damage and yes, our magical-swords did Agg. Our rules were out of blood + Seven Agg.-damage equals ash for the vampire. <br /> <br /> We never played 3rd edition V:tM, so for all damage it was Stamina + Fortitude for soak. We only played NWoD for a bit; werewolves seemed toned down, and vampires were limited, but, they weren't really. <br /> <br /> We used a lot of house-rules like, you add your successes for damage for even melee and brawling damage, which you were supposed to. I never liked that house-rule, so, in a Gladiator-game, the gladiators, could, add their successes to damage for their rolls if you had a specialty in that melee-weapon. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T05:13:40-07:00","id":1508736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508236#post1508236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really not sure if this was meant with irony in mind, but to be fair, as one friend of mine who loves <i>D&amp;D </i>a lot, in the WoD it's much more common to have possible antagonists that you definitely can't defeat than in other games. I'm saying that, because it sounded like perhaps you meant that ironically, in the sense that I should look more at other games (isn't Drachenfels from <i>Warhammer</i>?(besides being a famous hill in Germany lol)).<br /> <br /> In the WoD, most of the time players aren't expected to really defeat the &quot;big baddies&quot; like Mithras, Baba Yaga, Goratrix, Ur-Shulgi, etc. Some books even mention that explicitly, like <i>Rage Across Russia</i>, that mention that the werewolves from the PCs aren't expected to really deal with Baba Yaga and her Zmeis.</div> </div> </div> </div>To explain, as I was being rather simplistic before. Drachenfels is a novel where a rag-tag group of adventurers, led by a prince, and including a vampire, Genevieve, set out to destroy a Dark Lord, Constant Drachenfels who is reputed to be undefeatable.<br /> <br /> Their quest is succesful and the Prince goes on to much success. The story is about a playwright who, many years later, is commissioned to write a play about the quest. The original adventurers are assembled to provide material for the play which has it's opening night in the castle where Drachenfels was defeated.<br /> <br /> Shenanigans ensue...<br /> <br /> I thought this would be of interests because...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> while the adventurers defeat Drachenfels, all is not as it seems as the villain is not as defeated as he appears at first, and only on the night of the show things are finally resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> !!!MORE SPOILERS!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Drachenfels is relevant because we were discussing ways to account for undefeatable villains against unfailing protagonists. The novel works directly with this issue and takes the 'Dark Lord defeated by bold adventurers' theme and subverts it very strongly as befits the Warhammer Fantasy world. LAST CHANCE TO BACK OUT! In this case specifically, one of the adventurers ends up striking a bargain with the dark lord for fame and fortune in exchange for furthering the dark lords agenda at a later date. A similar 'bait and switch' plot device could also be used with many of the 'big bads' of the WoD canon to allow a player group to defeat them but ultimately ending in victory for the villain.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you haven't heard of him before Kim Newman's writing is very much suitable to the world of darkness, he's the author of the Anno Dracula series which I've found to be a great inspiration for my stories in WoD.<br /> <br /> References<br /> <a href=\"https://johnnyalucard.com/fiction/by-kim-newman/anno-dracula-series/\" target=\"_blank\">Anno Dracula Series | The Kim Newman Web Site (johnnyalucard.com)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://warhammerfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Constant_Drachenfels\" target=\"_blank\">Constant Drachenfels | Warhammer Wiki | Fandom</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://warhammerfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Genevieve_Dieudonn%C3%A9\" target=\"_blank\">Genevieve Dieudonn\u00e9 | Warhammer Wiki | Fandom</a>\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:16:18-07:00","id":1509278,"title":"","content":"So, I avoided reading your reply <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> because I decided to read the book, so I'm avoiding spoilers. The reading has been interesting so far, I'm going to reply once I finish reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T14:45:20-07:00","id":1509411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508583#post1508583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my thought as well. Unfortunately we see many instances in books where the coterie is almost predetermined to &quot;win&quot;, Darkening Sky is a good example by the way.<br /> <br /> Would you care to share any of your experiences with this kind of scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, one good thing to do in these sorts of scenarios is the following five tips.<br /> <br /> <b>Make it clear the player characters aren't necessarily in a life or death struggle</b>: Vampires should not necessarily be trying to kill the PCs. It's good to have player characters possibly in danger but the situation is often more likely games of cat and mouse for money, power, prestige, or position.<br /> <br /> <b>There's no good side</b>: Freddy vs. Jason so to speak. If Horatio Ballard is up against Al Capone with the PCs caught in the middle, then whoever wins is going to still be an asshole. So *A* villain is<br /> likely to be an ally.<br /> <br /> <b>Make the villain's victory good storytelling</b>: Players, not necessarily their characters, don't mind their characters suffering or failing as long as it's interesting. As long as it doesn't seem UNFAIR, tragic endings are appreciated rather than derided. This is a matter of opinion but if you avoid a &quot;cheap&quot; ending or diablous ex machina, most players will roll with it.<br /> <br /> Here's a short list of some things from various campaigns:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The System can't be Beaten</b>: Some humans find out about the existence of vampires and the player characters try to basically tell them how much their lives are in danger or to protect them. Some of them listen, others get their mind washed. One of the more likable ones ends up trying to go to the authorities and the PCs hear later that they were killed in a hit and run.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Stupid idealists get massacred</b>: Some Anarchs are determiend to declare a block of the city into a Free State and haven for Thin Bloods and Caitiff in their area. The player characters gave their protection when they were effectively running the city (Tampa Florida). When the PCs got overthrown for a time, they retuirn to find the area had been completely massacred.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>You got Palpatined</b>: The player characters got into a fight with another Anarch gang and the PCs never understood why he was so hateful to them. In the end, the two of them had a thrown down that resulted in the PCs triumphant, the Anarch leader dead, and a bloody triumph. The Prince then invites them to Elsyium and reveals that they would now have his territory. Because the PCs are told that the dead Anarch leader's sister had been murdered and somehow he thought the PCs were responsible (because the Prince framed them).<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Always a bigger fish</b>: The PCs get to witness a powerful godlike Methusaleh or Elder waltz into an area, slaughter everyone, and then walk out. The PCs are then offered positions by the figure and rewards but made clear that they are facing something simply beyond their kin.\u200b Basically, the PCs get offered a job by evil and thus become part of the villain's schemes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-26-2023, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:35:40-07:00","id":1509503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Make the villain's victory good storytelling</b>: Players, not necessarily their characters, don't mind their characters suffering or failing as long as it's interesting. As long as it doesn't seem UNFAIR, tragic endings are appreciated rather than derided. This is a matter of opinion but if you avoid a &quot;cheap&quot; ending or diablous ex machina, most players will role with it.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is surely by far the most important aspect of such situations. As long as it's good storytelling, I'm ok with most things. In all my games since I started ST (some 20+ years ago) I make it clear that the game is not D&amp;D and that the characters are in no way exempt from being destroyed (especially if they make stupid mistakes), etc. When I'm dealing with players who watch series I often tell them that it's more like <i>GoT </i>or with gamers I jokingly say it's more like <i>Dark Souls</i> than Final Fantasy lol. I usually don't hear much complaining when they lose their characters, as I said the post is more to discuss this theme, because even though I don't usually run into problems with situations like this, often when I'm reading Official Material for the WoD, I see a very &quot;lenient&quot; approach suggested by the books, even in scenarios where the characters should surely face the danger of being destroyed, the books generally advise the ST to be much more &quot;lenient&quot; than I'm used to be. So it often makes me curious regarding other people's experience as ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T19:26:00-07:00","id":1509542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1508736#post1508736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To explain, as I was being rather simplistic before. Drachenfels is a novel where a rag-tag group of adventurers, led by a prince, and including a vampire, Genevieve, set out to destroy a Dark Lord, Constant Drachenfels who is reputed to be undefeatable.<br /> <br /> Their quest is succesful and the Prince goes on to much success. The story is about a playwright who, many years later, is commissioned to write a play about the quest. The original adventurers are assembled to provide material for the play which has it's opening night in the castle where Drachenfels was defeated.<br /> <br /> Shenanigans ensue...<br /> <br /> I thought this would be of interests because...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> !!!SPOILERS AHEAD!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> while the adventurers defeat Drachenfels, all is not as it seems as the villain is not as defeated as he appears at first, and only on the night of the show things are finally resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> !!!MORE SPOILERS!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Drachenfels is relevant because we were discussing ways to account for undefeatable villains against unfailing protagonists. The novel works directly with this issue and takes the 'Dark Lord defeated by bold adventurers' theme and subverts it very strongly as befits the Warhammer Fantasy world. LAST CHANCE TO BACK OUT! In this case specifically, one of the adventurers ends up striking a bargain with the dark lord for fame and fortune in exchange for furthering the dark lords agenda at a later date. A similar 'bait and switch' plot device could also be used with many of the 'big bads' of the WoD canon to allow a player group to defeat them but ultimately ending in victory for the villain.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you haven't heard of him before Kim Newman's writing is very much suitable to the world of darkness, he's the author of the Anno Dracula series which I've found to be a great inspiration for my stories in WoD.<br /> <br /> References<br /> <a href=\"https://johnnyalucard.com/fiction/by-kim-newman/anno-dracula-series/\" target=\"_blank\">Anno Dracula Series | The Kim Newman Web Site (johnnyalucard.com)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://warhammerfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Constant_Drachenfels\" target=\"_blank\">Constant Drachenfels | Warhammer Wiki | Fandom</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://warhammerfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Genevieve_Dieudonn%C3%A9\" target=\"_blank\">Genevieve Dieudonn\u00e9 | Warhammer Wiki | Fandom</a>\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I finally had time to finish reading the book. It was a good reading, even though I must say the end was very disappointing, because it made absolutely no sense to have Detlef become a kind of reincarnation of Sigmar in that fight with Drachenfels. It's a pity, because I loved the book until that point, especially what you mentioned, that in reality Oswald had struck a deal with Drachenfels, etc, that part was masterfully done and gave me many good ideas, as it reminded me of the way the WoD works. But then after that it became really cringy, because everything in that fight felt EXTREMELY forced, how was Detlef supposed to summon that strength out of nowhere, the hammer glowing, etc, the narrative up until that point had led the reader to believe Drachencels was completely out of the group's league, the end felt like some situations I've seen in RPGs where the ST (usually one without much experience) feels so desperate because he doesn't want the group to be mad at him for losing their characters and then decides to resource to <i>Deus ex machina</i> just in order to make the group succeed, however forced that feels, something I've always abhorred in books, games, as well as in TV shows, series, films, etc.<br /> <br /> In any case, the reading was surely worth it. Thank you for the book recommendation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T00:56:50-07:00","id":1509694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1509542#post1509542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then after that it became really cringy, because everything in that fight felt EXTREMELY forced, how was Detlef supposed to summon that strength out of nowhere, the hammer glowing, etc, the narrative up until that point had led the reader to believe Drachencels was completely out of the group's league</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the feeling that it was a required part of the plot imposed by the publisher/Games Workshop in order to fit the higher goals of the game world<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T06:35:28-07:00","id":1509712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507262-have-you-ever-had-your-villain-win-scenario?p=1509694#post1509694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the feeling that it was a required part of the plot imposed by the publisher/Games Workshop in order to fit the higher goals of the game world<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have a similar feeling as well, because it felt so forced that it was like suddenly there was another narrator/storyteller/writer there. But until that point I thought the story was marvelous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}